  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Action Against Desertification (A Component)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The specific objective of the project is to improve the condition and productivity of the agro-sylvo-pastoral landscapes affected by desertification, land degradation and drought (DLDD) in Africa, Carribbean and Pacific (ACP) countries through the implementation of the GGWSSI in six African countries and South-South cooperation in ACP Countries. The project will aim at achieving the following results: br  (i) Enhanced enabling environment and capacity of relevant governmental and non-governmental institutions and stakeholders in terms of effective cross-sectoral work, planning, financing, budgeting, implementation, monitoring and evaluation of sustainable land/forest management and restoration at a landscape level; br  (ii) Local communities, governmental and non-governmental stakeholders (including youth, women and civil society) in selected landscape units have adopted and are using improved sustainable land/forest management practices and technologies, as part of the implementation of their Great Green Wall Action Plans ; br  (iii) Knowledge and awareness are enhanced among key target audiences and stakeholders from the European Union and ACP countries regarding the causes of and appropriate measures to combat desertification and land degradation and improve resilience to climate change while promoting sustainable livelihoods. br 
South- South Cooperation will be at the hea</narrative>
  </description>
